# PLACEHOLDER — rename to vault-allowlist.conf and fill in before the Vault host goes live.
#
# H5 in MIGRATION_AWS_PLAN.md §5: "Office static IP(s) / VPN for the Vault allow-list." Nobody
# has supplied one yet, so this file ships as a REFUSAL rather than a guess — an empty `allow
# all;` here would be silently equivalent to no allow-list at all, on the one host in this
# topology whose entire security model is "reachable only via allow-list" (§109.3 / SB-04).
#
# Once H5 is answered, replace the contents of vault-allowlist.conf (not this file) with:
#
#   allow 203.0.113.10;       # example office static IP — REPLACE
#   allow 203.0.113.0/28;     # example office CIDR — REPLACE
#   # allow <VPN egress IP/CIDR>;
#   deny all;
#
# and reference it from infra/aws/nginx/vault.conf's `location /` (and every other location that
# is not the ACME challenge path) with `include /etc/nginx/rawprod/vault-allowlist.conf;`. The
# security group in front of this host (MIGRATION_AWS_PLAN.md §3 B4, SG `vault-web`) is the
# OTHER half of this control, not a substitute for it — a security group is IP-based too, but a
# change to one is not a change to the other, and both are meant to say the same thing.
#
# Until this file is replaced, infra/aws/nginx/vault.conf's own placeholder `deny all;` (see that
# file) keeps the console unreachable rather than reachable-by-accident.
